# Stop the DiskOnChip driver loading, on a machine that has no DiskOnChip.
#
# `trueffs.dll` is the TrueFFS driver for the DiskOnChip flash the real board
# carries. This one does not have one: it was removed deliberately, and
# `\Flash Disk` comes from the SD card instead. `crates/gandalf/src/lib.rs`
# answers the two chip selects it lives on with all ones, on the reasoning
# that ones are what an empty bus looks like and zeroes are what a sick chip
# looks like, so ones would make it give up.
#
# Measured, it does not give up. `--sample-pc` over a run puts about fifteen
# percent of the machine's time inside this DLL, spread across a handful of
# addresses around `trueffs.dll+0x3fc00` -- a probe loop, running for ever,
# for hardware that will never answer. That is fifteen percent taken from
# every boot and every keystroke on an interpreter that is already the
# slowest part of this project.
#
# So it is not given the chance. The registry entry that loads it names the
# file, and this changes that name to one that is not in the ROM: the loader
# looks for `trueffs.off`, does not find it, gives up, and moves on to the
# next driver. Nothing else in the image refers to the file -- the name
# occurs exactly once -- and nothing depends on the driver, because there is
# no device under it.
#
# The name is the same length, so no record grows and no offset moves.
#
# The `Dll` value name is carried in front of the filename in the signature.
# `trueffs.dll` is unique on its own, but matching the pair means this can
# only ever fire on a value that really is telling the loader what to load.

name: no DiskOnChip driver
because: it polls for hardware this machine does not have, for 15% of its time
reach: sole
at: 8

signature:
  44 00 6c 00 6c 00 00 00                           # "Dll" and its terminator
  74 00 72 00 75 00 65 00 66 00 66 00 73 00 2e 00   # "trueffs."
  64 00 6c 00 6c 00 00 00                           # "dll" and its terminator

replacement:
  74 00 72 00 75 00 65 00 66 00 66 00 73 00 2e 00   # "trueffs."
  6f 00 66 00 66 00                                 # "off", so nothing loads
